{"black_box_warning":{"current_value":"Long boxed warning text for cardiovascular risk associated with rapid infusion rates, with DailyMed listed as the source.","fda_source_urls":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%22d4c36fad-0ba2-4cd4-9c5e-dcf843f38a5a%22&limit=5","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2019/020450s039lbl.pdf"],"proposed_value":"No boxed-warning text change required; replace the source metadata with an FDA/openFDA or accessdata FDA label source, not DailyMed.","rationale":"FDA labeling verifies a boxed warning for cardiovascular risk associated with rapid IV infusion rates. The current warning source is not acceptable for this field because it cites DailyMed.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified"},"blocking_questions":[],"fact_checks":[{"current_value":"Neurologic: nystagmus 44%, CNS: dizziness 31%, dermatologic: pruritus 27%, neurologic: ataxia 25%, CNS: somnolence 17%, cardiovascular: hypotension 8%","field":"adverse_symptoms_percentages","proposed_value":"Neurologic: nystagmus 44%, CNS: dizziness 31%, dermatologic: pruritus 49%, CNS: somnolence 20%, neurologic: ataxia 11%, cardiovascular: hypotension 8%","rationale":"FDA label Table 1 supports nystagmus 44%, dizziness 31%, somnolence 20%, ataxia 11%, pruritus 49%, and hypotension 8% for IV CEREBYX at maximum dose/rate; current pruritus, ataxia, and somnolence percentages do not match.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2019/020450s039lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"","field":"alternate_generic_names","proposed_value":"fosphenytoin sodium","rationale":"FDA and eMC sources use fosphenytoin sodium as the active/generic salt name; it should be listed as an alias of fosphenytoin, not as a separate drug row.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"missing","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2019/020450s039lbl.pdf","https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/medicine/13310/SPC/pro-epanutin%20concentrate%20for%20infusion%20~%20solution%20for%20injection"]},{"current_value":"Yes","field":"available_in_us","proposed_value":"Yes","rationale":"CEREBYX/fosphenytoin sodium is FDA-labeled and FDA-approved in the United States.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2019/020450s039lbl.pdf","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK547879/"]},{"current_value":"Phenytoin prodrug; strong CYP/UGT enzyme inducer after conversion","field":"enzyme_inducing_or_inhibiting","proposed_value":"Phenytoin prodrug; potent inducer of hepatic drug-metabolizing enzymes after conversion","rationale":"FDA labeling supports that phenytoin/CEREBYX is a potent inducer of hepatic drug-metabolizing enzymes, but the row's specific CYP/UGT wording is not directly supported by the cited FDA label text.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"missing_source","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2019/020450s039lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Status epilepticus; Focal; Generalized tonic-clonic","field":"epilepsy_type","proposed_value":"Status epilepticus; Focal; Generalized tonic-clonic","rationale":"FDA labeling directly supports generalized tonic-clonic status epilepticus and short-term substitution for oral phenytoin; focal use is supported indirectly via phenytoin substitution/indications, so the retained value needs the proposed expanded evidence sources.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2019/020450s039lbl.pdf","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK547879/","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK548889/"]},{"current_value":"NCBI LiverTox anticonvulsants table; FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"NCBI LiverTox fosphenytoin/phenytoin records; FDA/accessdata CEREBYX prescribing information; eMC Pro-Epanutin SmPC; PubMed and ClinicalTrials.gov records for RCT/trial fields","rationale":"Current source text uses DailyMed and omits eMC for Pro-Epanutin and trial sources for RCT-specific fields.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK547879/","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK548889/","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2019/020450s039lbl.pdf","https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/medicine/13310/SPC/pro-epanutin%20concentrate%20for%20infusion%20~%20solution%20for%20injection","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24135012/","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT01870024"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed SPL; status=boxed_warning_found; setid=d4c36fad-0ba2-4cd4-9c5e-dcf843f38a5a; published=Aug 29, 2025; title=CEREBYX (FOSPHENYTOIN SODIUM) INJECTION, SOLUTION [PFIZER LABORATORIES DIV PFIZER INC]; url=https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=d4c36fad-0ba2-4cd4-9c5e-dcf843f38a5a","field":"fda_black_box_warning_source","proposed_value":"FDA/openFDA drug label API; status=boxed_warning_found; spl_set_id=d4c36fad-0ba2-4cd4-9c5e-dcf843f38a5a; effective_time=20250828; title=CEREBYX / FOSPHENYTOIN SODIUM; api_url=https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%22d4c36fad-0ba2-4cd4-9c5e-dcf843f38a5a%22&limit=5","rationale":"DailyMed is not permissible for boxed-warning verification under the audit rules; use FDA/openFDA or FDA label metadata.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%22d4c36fad-0ba2-4cd4-9c5e-dcf843f38a5a%22&limit=5","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2019/020450s039lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"IV/IM injection","field":"formulations_available","proposed_value":"IV/IM injection","rationale":"FDA labeling and eMC SmPC describe fosphenytoin/CEREBYX/Pro-Epanutin for intravenous or intramuscular administration.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2019/020450s039lbl.pdf","https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/medicine/13310/SPC/pro-epanutin%20concentrate%20for%20infusion%20~%20solution%20for%20injection"]},{"current_value":"Conversion ~15 min; phenytoin ~7-42 h","field":"half_life_range","proposed_value":"Conversion ~15 min; derived phenytoin mean total half-life 12.0-28.9 h after CEREBYX at studied doses","rationale":"FDA CEREBYX labeling supports fosphenytoin conversion half-life of about 15 minutes and mean total phenytoin half-life values of 12.0-28.9 hours after CEREBYX. The 7-42 hour range is a general oral phenytoin range, not concordant with the cited CEREBYX FDA label.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2019/020450s039lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Plasma phosphatases convert prodrug; phenytoin metabolized in liver","field":"major_organ_for_metabolism","proposed_value":"Phosphatases convert fosphenytoin to phenytoin; derived phenytoin is extensively metabolized in the liver by CYP2C9 and CYP2C19","rationale":"FDA label says the conversion mechanism has not been determined but phosphatases probably play a major role, and derived phenytoin is extensively metabolized in the liver by CYP2C9/CYP2C19. The current 'plasma phosphatases' wording is too specific for the cited label.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2019/020450s039lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Loading 20 mg PE/kg; maintenance typically 4-6 mg PE/kg/day","field":"maximum_approved_daily_dose","proposed_value":"Loading 20 mg PE/kg; maintenance typically 4-6 mg PE/kg/day","rationale":"FDA labeling supports status epilepticus loading dose 15-20 mg PE/kg and adult maintenance 4-6 mg PE/kg/day.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2019/020450s039lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Moderate","field":"mechanism_confidence","proposed_value":"Moderate","rationale":"FDA label states the precise mechanism of phenytoin's therapeutic effect has not been established but is thought to involve voltage-dependent sodium-channel blockade, supporting moderate confidence.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2019/020450s039lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Phenytoin prodrug; anticonvulsant effects are attributable to phenytoin, whose mechanism is not established but is thought to involve voltage-dependent sodium-channel blockade.","field":"mechanism_of_action","proposed_value":"Phenytoin prodrug; anticonvulsant effects are attributable to phenytoin, whose mechanism is not established but is thought to involve voltage-dependent sodium-channel blockade.","rationale":"FDA label directly supports this mechanism statement.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2019/020450s039lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"mechanism_source","proposed_value":"FDA/accessdata CEREBYX prescribing information","rationale":"DailyMed is not in the trusted source list provided for this audit; the same mechanism is supported by FDA/accessdata labeling.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2019/020450s039lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA label","field":"mechanism_source_tier","proposed_value":"FDA label","rationale":"The mechanism is supported by FDA prescribing information.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2019/020450s039lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Loading/maintenance depends on indication; acute efficacy is not expressed as a chronic daily minimum","field":"minimum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"Loading/maintenance depends on indication; acute efficacy is not expressed as a chronic daily minimum","rationale":"FDA labeling provides indication-specific loading and maintenance regimens and therapeutic monitoring rather than a chronic daily minimum effective dose.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2019/020450s039lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"","field":"pubmed_search_aliases","proposed_value":"fosphenytoin sodium; Cerebyx; Pro-Epanutin; Sesquient","rationale":"Search aliases should include the salt name and major trade names so alias rows are not created separately.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"missing","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2019/020450s039lbl.pdf","https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/medicine/13310/SPC/pro-epanutin%20concentrate%20for%20infusion%20~%20solution%20for%20injection","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/nda/2021/210864Orig1s000OtherR.pdf"]},{"current_value":"No typical QT prolongation; IV administration can cause hypotension/arrhythmias","field":"qt_interval_effect","proposed_value":"QT interval prolongation has been reported infrequently; IV administration can cause hypotension and cardiac arrhythmias, especially with rapid infusion","rationale":"FDA labeling lists QT interval prolongation as an infrequent cardiovascular adverse event and carries a boxed warning for hypotension/cardiac arrhythmias with rapid IV infusion. The current 'No typical QT prolongation' wording is not directly supported by the cited label.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2019/020450s039lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Cerebyx; Pro-Epanutin","field":"trade_names","proposed_value":"Cerebyx; Pro-Epanutin; Sesquient","rationale":"Cerebyx is FDA-labeled, Pro-Epanutin is an eMC/UK SmPC trade name, and FDA review material identifies Sesquient as a fosphenytoin sodium product; all should be aliases of fosphenytoin, not separate generic rows.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"missing","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2019/020450s039lbl.pdf","https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/medicine/13310/SPC/pro-epanutin%20concentrate%20for%20infusion%20~%20solution%20for%20injection","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/nda/2021/210864Orig1s000OtherR.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Status/loading: 15-20 mg PE/kg; maintenance 4-6 mg PE/kg/day when used","field":"typical_doses_per_day","proposed_value":"Status/loading: 15-20 mg PE/kg; maintenance 4-6 mg PE/kg/day when used","rationale":"FDA labeling supports 15-20 mg PE/kg for status epilepticus loading and 4-6 mg PE/kg/day adult maintenance dosing.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2019/020450s039lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"1996","field":"year_fda_cleared","proposed_value":"1996","rationale":"FDA label highlights and NCBI LiverTox both support initial U.S. approval/use approval in 1996.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2019/020450s039lbl.pdf","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK547879/"]}],"generic_name":"fosphenytoin","missing_rcts":[{"pmid":"8759983","proposed_link_text":"Wilder1996|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8759983/","title":"Safety and tolerance of multiple doses of intramuscular fosphenytoin substituted for oral phenytoin in epilepsy or neurosurgery","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8759983/","why_relevant":"Potential missing PubMed RCT: PubMed abstract verifies randomized double-dummy/placebo-controlled fosphenytoin substitution in epilepsy/neurosurgery patients. Phase II