onversion ~15 min; derived phenytoin mean total half-life 12.0-28.9 h after CEREBYX at studied doses","reason":"Align PK range with FDA CEREBYX label.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2019/020450s039lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Plasma phosphatases convert prodrug; phenytoin metabolized in liver","field":"major_organ_for_metabolism","proposed_value":"Phosphatases convert fosphenytoin to phenytoin; derived phenytoin is extensively metabolized in the liver by CYP2C9 and CYP2C19","reason":"FDA label supports phosphatases generally and hepatic CYP2C9/CYP2C19 metabolism of derived phenytoin.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2019/020450s039lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"mechanism_source","proposed_value":"FDA/accessdata CEREBYX prescribing information","reason":"Replace DailyMed with FDA/accessdata source wording.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2019/020450s039lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"","field":"pubmed_search_aliases","proposed_value":"fosphenytoin sodium; Cerebyx; Pro-Epanutin; Sesquient","reason":"Add search aliases/trade names to prevent duplicate alias rows.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2019/020450s039lbl.pdf","https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/medicine/13310/SPC/pro-epanutin%20concentrate%20for%20infusion%20~%20solution%20for%20injection","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/nda/2021/210864Orig1s000OtherR.pdf"]},{"current_value":"No typical QT prolongation; IV administration can cause hypotension/arrhythmias","field":"qt_interval_effect","proposed_value":"QT interval prolongation has been reported infrequently; IV administration can cause hypotension and cardiac arrhythmias, especially with rapid infusion","reason":"FDA label reports QT interval prolongation as infrequent and includes cardiovascular boxed warning.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2019/020450s039lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Cerebyx; Pro-Epanutin","field":"trade_names","proposed_value":"Cerebyx; Pro-Epanutin; Sesquient","reason":"Add FDA-identified Sesquient trade alias while retaining Cerebyx and Pro-Epanutin.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2019/020450s039lbl.pdf","https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/medicine/13310/SPC/pro-epanutin%20concentrate%20for%20infusion%20~%20solution%20for%20injection","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/nda/2021/210864Orig1s000OtherR.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Gwer2013|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24135012/","field":"pubmed_phase_ii_iii_rct_links","proposed_value":"Gwer2013|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24135012/; Wilder1996|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8759983/","reason":"Wilder1996 was not merely a title-only drug hit; PubMed abstract describes randomized double-dummy/placebo-controlled IM fosphenytoin substitution. Add only if non-efficacy safety/substitution placebo RCTs are in this field's scope because phase is not explicit.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8759983/"]},{"current_value":"PubMed loop 23/65 on 2026-05-15: 1 qualifying placebo-controlled randomized clinical trial report(s) retained from 3 PubMed candidate(s). Links were rebuilt from fetched PubMed PMID metadata and named FirstAuthorYear. Differential effectiveness columns summarize extractable maximum effective dose/regimen values within qualifying RCT reports.","field":"rct_pubmed_verification_notes","proposed_value":"Audit 2026-05-20: Gwer2013 (PMID 24135012) is a randomized double-blind placebo-controlled fosphenytoin 20 mg PE/kg IM seizure-prevention trial in childhood acute coma; PubMed phase is not explicit and it does not report RR50/MPC/seizure-freedom efficacy endpoints. Wilder1996 (PMID 8759983) is a randomized double-dummy placebo-controlled safety/tolerability/PK substitution trial of IM fosphenytoin in epilepsy/neurosurgery; include only if non-efficacy safety/substitution RCTs are in scope. ClinicalTrials.gov NCT01870024 is a completed phase 3 randomized double-blind status-epilepticus trial with placebo infusion arms and a fosphenytoin arm but no linked PubMed results identified.","reason":"Clarify RCT scope, phase uncertainty, non-extractable outcomes, and trial registry finding.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24135012/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8759983/","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT01870024"]}],"rct_link_checks":[{"label":"Gwer2013","pmid":"24135012","proposed_action":"Retain as a placebo-controlled randomized fosphenytoin seizure-prevention trial, but update notes because PubMed does not explicitly verify phase II/III and the trial does not report standard RR50/MPC/seizure-freedom endpoints.","rationale":"The cited article is for fosphenytoin, randomized, double-blind, and placebo-controlled, but phase II/III status is not explicit in the PubMed-level evidence available. It reports seizure occurrence in childhood coma prophylaxis rather than chronic epilepsy responder outcomes.","status":"insufficient_evidence","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24135012/"}],"source_updates":[{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed SPL; status=boxed_warning_found; setid=d4c36fad-0ba2-4cd4-9c5e-dcf843f38a5a; published=Aug 29, 2025; title=CEREBYX (FOSPHENYTOIN SODIUM) INJECTION, SOLUTION [PFIZER LABORATORIES DIV PFIZER INC]; url=https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=d4c36fad-0ba2-4cd4-9c5e-dcf843f38a5a","field":"fda_black_box_warning_source","proposed_value":"FDA/openFDA drug label API; status=boxed_warning_found; spl_set_id=d4c36fad-0ba2-4cd4-9c5e-dcf843f38a5a; effective_time=20250828; title=CEREBYX / FOSPHENYTOIN SODIUM; api_url=https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%22d4c36fad-0ba2-4cd4-9c5e-dcf843f38a5a%22&limit=5","reason":"Boxed warning source must be FDA/openFDA/FDA label/Drugs@FDA, not DailyMed.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%22d4c36fad-0ba2-4cd4-9c5e-dcf843f38a5a%22&limit=5","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2019/020450s039lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"mechanism_source","proposed_value":"FDA/accessdata CEREBYX prescribing information","reason":"Use trusted FDA label source naming.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2019/020450s039lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"NCBI LiverTox anticonvulsants table; FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"NCBI LiverTox fosphenytoin/phenytoin records; FDA/accessdata CEREBYX prescribing information; eMC Pro-Epanutin SmPC; PubMed and ClinicalTrials.gov records for RCT/trial fields","reason":"Current named sources do not support all trade-name and RCT-specific facts and include DailyMed wording.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK547879/","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK548889/","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2019/020450s039lbl.pdf","https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/medicine/13310/SPC/pro-epanutin%20concentrate%20for%20infusion%20~%20solution%20for%20injection","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24135012/","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT01870024"]}],"summary":"Row needs updates. FDA/accessdata supports core availability, indication, formulation, dosing, mechanism, 1996 approval, and boxed warning, but the black-box source must be changed away from DailyMed. Adverse-event percentages, half-life wording, metabolism wording, QT wording, aliases/trade names, and source metadata need correction. Gwer2013 is a fosphenytoin placebo RCT but phase is not explicit and standard RR50/MPC/seizure-freedom outcomes remain not extractable."}
